cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Lattice"
abstract: >-
  Lattice is a deterministic multi-agent environment for auditable agent
  benchmarking: every run is seeded, every recording is hash-verified on replay,
  and negative results are published as first-class evidence.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mehta
    given-names: Deep
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/candavere/lattice"
version: 3.1.0
# date-released is intentionally omitted. Under CFF 1.2.0 it is optional and
# means the date the software was released. 3.1.0 is not released yet: there is
# no v3.1.0 tag, no GitHub Release, and no published package. The field is
# filled in at the tagging/publication step, which is a separate, separately
# approved action, and it must record that step's real date -- not a planned or
# assumed one. The last actual release date, for v3.0.0, was 2026-09-27; it
# belongs to that version and is not a claim about 3.1.0.
